<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shihab dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shihabs, Chehab family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shihab dynasty were an Arab family who ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-lebanon">Mount Lebanon</a> under Ottoman suzerainty from 1697 to 1842, succeeding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/man-dynasty">Ma'n dynasty</a>. Originally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> Muslims from Wadi al-Taym, some of them later became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maronites">Maronite Christians</a>. The emirate reached its height under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bashir-shihab-ii">Bashir Shihab II</a>, whose fall in 1840 was followed by civil strife and the end of the emirate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shihab-dynasty.jpg" alt="Shihab dynasty" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Santiago Dotor Vector: Connormah · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chehab_family_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
